# See http://help.github.com/ignore-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# TLS certificates (infrastructure/docker/scripts/generate-internal-certs.sh)
certs/

# perf-baseline JSON outputs (noise; markdown summary is the durable artefact)
docs/perf/runs/

# Dependencies
node_modules

# Build outputs
dist
build
tmp
out-tsc
static
.nx/

# Exception: tools/eslint-rules/dist/ is COMMITTED.
# Workspace-local ESLint plugin resolved via `plugins: ["aquaculture"]`
# in .eslintrc.json. Because CI uses `npm install --ignore-scripts`
# (SEC-CI-007 supply-chain hygiene), the package's `prepare` script
# does NOT run on install, so dist/ would be empty on a fresh runner.
# Every Nx-invoking job (install graph probe, build-backend-artifacts,
# build-frontend-artifacts) would then crash with "Cannot find module
# 'eslint-plugin-aquaculture'". Rather than add a runtime build step
# to every job (recursive patching), we commit dist/ and enforce
# source/dist parity via the `eslint-rules-dist-drift` CI gate.
!tools/eslint-rules/dist/
!tools/eslint-rules/dist/**

